// Z3 Contract Test: a function's own `requires` must be assumed as a fact
// while verifying calls IT makes to other functions.
// Expected: PASS
//
// `requires { x <= LIMIT }` parses as Expr::Block. caller_preconditions was
// correctly pushed/popped around the function body and correctly consumed
// at the callee-requires check site -- but translate_bool_to_z3 has no arm
// for Expr::Block, so every entry silently failed to translate and never
// reached the solver. `requires(x <= LIMIT)` (paren form) was never
// affected, which is why this stayed hidden: the plumbing looked complete
// end to end, and the paren form exercised it correctly.
package test_composability_requires_proved

const LIMIT: u64 = 100;

fn g(x: u64) requires { x <= LIMIT } { }

pub fn f(x: u64) requires { x <= LIMIT } {
    g(x);
}
